Q: Explain one real-world use case where exposing a local application is useful.

ANS :

The local application was exposed to the internet using ngrok. The application was running on port 8080, and ngrok created a public HTTPS URL that forwarded requests to the local application.

Local application:
    http://localhost:8080

Public URL:
    https://credibly-alone-astound.ngrok-free.dev/

Command used:
    ngrok http 8080

Real-world use case:
    Exposing a local application is useful when a developer needs to share a work-in-progress application with a client, teammate, tester, or instructor without deploying it to a production server.

    For example, a developer can run an application locally and use ngrok to give a tester a temporary public URL. The tester can access the application from another network and provide feedback.